{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018NDuaipAXqAGhkWqiYCwqL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CommunityConnect 2025 Scoring Rubric for Abstracts 5 Excellent 4 Good 3 Fair 2\",\"url\":\"https://irp.cdn-website.com/9100a73e/files/uploaded/2025_Reviewer_Rating_Form_(Workshop_Rubric).pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning), but the results primarily show information from CoRL 2023 and 2024, along with some 2026 data. The search did not return specific detailed information about the CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric.\n\nFrom what I found:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers are generally asked to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nHowever, for the complete and specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, review form, and detailed scoring rubric, you may want to check the official CoRL 2025 OpenReview page or the CoRL website directly, as the detailed scoring criteria for the 2025 conference were not fully captured in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"24a48b7a-5d3f-4e33-b2d1-2b87013a64e5","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:33:32.859Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011ZK4ShpDo6NWthcW9QfrMg","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"ICLR 2025 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CommunityConnect 2025 Scoring Rubric for Abstracts 5 Excellent 4 Good 3 Fair 2","url":"https://irp.cdn-website.com/9100a73e/files/uploaded/2025_Reviewer_Rating_Form_(Workshop_Rubric).pdf"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning), but the results primarily show information from CoRL 2023 and 2024, along with some 2026 data. The search did not return specific detailed information about the CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines review form scoring rubric.\n\nFrom what I found:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by authors should be pointed out extensively and strongly reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers are generally asked to be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements, while making reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical.\n\nHowever, for the complete and specific CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines, review form, and detailed scoring rubric, you may want to check the official CoRL 2025 OpenReview page or the CoRL website directly, as the detailed scoring criteria for the 2025 conference were not fully captured in these search results."],"durationSeconds":5.567950655999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CNUMYW4dnmgwDT3KEY6MFv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to CoRL 2026, though specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines appear to be under development. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Review Information\n\nThe search results show that CoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper, and accepted papers and reviews will be publicly accessible and de-anonymized after decisions are announced.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent 