{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A5sxp1Y5T5GA8PQC33PP4X","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the complete review form scoring scale/rubric is not included** in this document.\n\n## What IS Provided:\n\n**Review Criteria:** Papers are evaluated on:\n- \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Objective establishment and potential for scientific/technological impact\n- Relevance to robotic learning\n\n**Scope Requirements:** Submissions must demonstrate robot learning relevance through either:\n- \"Intent: Explicitly address a learning question for physical robots OR\"\n- \"Outcome: Test the proposed learning solution on physical robots\"\n\n## What IS NOT Provided:\n\n1. **Overall score rating scale** – no numerical or categorical scoring levels are detailed\n2. **Scored dimensions** (soundness, significance, novelty, clarity) – no rubrics for these categories\n3. **Acceptance rate** – not mentioned\n4. **Accept/reject thresholds** – no specific guidance on score cutoffs or decision criteria\n\n---\n\n**Note:** This page contains instructions for reviewer qualifications and desk rejection criteria, but the actual review form with scoring scales appears to be hosted elsewhere or provided separately to reviewers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"5b1b3da1-0788-4917-9278-2ba6fce2ed90","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:34:19.316Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":134169,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2024 Review Form Analysis\n\nBased on the provided webpage content, **the complete review form scoring scale/rubric is not included** in this document.\n\n## What IS Provided:\n\n**Review Criteria:** Papers are evaluated on:\n- \"significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical\"\n- Objective establishment and potential for scientific/technological impact\n- Relevance to robotic learning\n\n**Scope Requirements:** Submissions must demonstrate robot learning relevance through either:\n- \"Intent: Explicitly address a learning question for physical robots OR\"\n- \"Outcome: Test the proposed learning solution on physical robots\"\n\n## What IS NOT Provided:\n\n1. **Overall score rating scale** – no numerical or categorical scoring levels are detailed\n2. **Scored dimensions** (soundness, significance, novelty, clarity) – no rubrics for these categories\n3. **Acceptance rate** – not mentioned\n4. **Accept/reject thresholds** – no specific guidance on score cutoffs or decision criteria\n\n---\n\n**Note:** This page contains instructions for reviewer qualifications and desk rejection criteria, but the actual review form with scoring scales appears to be hosted elsewhere or provided separately to reviewers.","durationMs":3919,"url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWFDhk4c4osJDnpu1RV1FD","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Scoring Scale\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form scoring scale or rubric. The document provides **review writing guidelines** but does not include:\n\n1. **Overall score rating scale** - No numerical or categorical scoring levels are specified\n2. **Scored dimensions with scales** - While the guidelines mention evaluation criteria (originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance, limitations), no corresponding scoring scales are provided\n3. **Acceptance rate** - Not mentioned in the document\n4. **Specific accept vs. reject thresholds** - Not defined\n\n## What IS Provided\n\nThe guidelines request reviewers to evaluate papers across six dimensions:\n\n- Originality (novelty of problems/methods)\n- Quality (technical soundness)\n- Clarity (writing and organization)\n- Significance (importance of results)\n- Relevance (relation to robot learning)\n- Limitations (honest assessment of shortcomings)\n\nHowever, the actual scoring mechanism, numerical scales, and decision criteria are absent from this page. This information likely exists in the OpenReview system itself or in technical instructions sent separately to reviewers."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"c8cbcdc1-80f9-4af8-af56-f9e87b324b3f","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:34:20.650Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":105095,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL 2023 Review Form Scoring Scale\n\nBased on the provided content, I cannot extract a complete review form scoring scale or rubric. The document provides **review writing guidelines** but does not include:\n\n1. **Overall score rating scale** - No numerical or categorical scoring levels are specified\n2. **Scored dimensions with scales** - While the guidelines mention evaluation criteria (originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance, limitations), no corresponding scoring scales are provided\n3. **Acceptance rate** - Not mentioned in the document\n4. **Specific accept vs. reject thresholds** - Not defined\n\n## What IS Provided\n\nThe guidelines request reviewers to evaluate papers across six dimensions:\n\n- Originality (novelty of problems/methods)\n- Quality (technical soundness)\n- Clarity (writing and organization)\n- Significance (importance of results)\n- Relevance (relation to robot learning)\n- Limitations (honest assessment of shortcomings)\n\nHowever, the actual scoring mechanism, numerical scales, and decision criteria are absent from this page. This information likely exists in the OpenReview system itself or in technical instructions sent separately to reviewers.","durationMs":4733,"url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"}}
