{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ag2u13QfsqbzKFzsVCcLTu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Data Summary — diff_collision_sdf\n2\t\n3\tGenerated: 2026-05-24 | Source: experiment registry (51 entries)\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Table 1: Pi0.5 + A1 — 3-seed × 2-lambda 结果矩阵\n8\t\n9\t10K mid-eval 数据来源：ROADMAP D016（手动 eval）\n10\t\n11\t| | λ=0.005 TSR | λ=0.005 CAR | λ=0.005 SSR | λ=0.01 TSR | λ=0.01 CAR | λ=0.01 SSR |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| seed 0 (10K) | 47% | 58% | 0% frozen | 49% | 56.5% | 0% frozen |\n14\t| seed 1 (30K) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |\n15\t| seed 2 (30K) | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD | TBD |\n16\t| **mean±std** | — | — | — | — | — | — |\n17\t\n18\t**对比基线：**\n19\t- Pi0.5 baseline 3-seed: TSR = 74.7 ± 1.5%, CAR = 26.8 ± 1.6% (n=600, seeds 7/1/2)\n20\t- Pi0.5 baseline per-seed: s0(seed7): TSR=73%, CAR=28% | s1: TSR=76%, CAR=25% | s2: TSR=75%, CAR=27.5%\n21\t\n22\t**分析：**\n23\t- A1 training 显著降低了 TSR（74.7% → 47-49%），但大幅提升了 CAR（26.8% → 56-58%）\n24\t- SSR=0% frozen 表明 A1 不产生 action collapse（与 Pi0 系方法的 99%+ fake safe 形成对比）\n25\t- seed 1/2 训练完成（30K steps）但因 SSH auth failure 未获取 eval metrics，需补跑 eval\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## Table 2 (Claim 1): Fake Safety 统计\n30\t\n31\t**核心论点：** 现有碰撞避免方法的高 CAR 是 \"fake safety\"——模型通过 action collapse（停止运动）而非真正的轨迹修正来避免碰撞。\n32\t\n33\t| Method | Episodes | TSR | CAR | Real Safe Rate | Fake Safe Rate | Source |\n34\t|--------|----------|-----|-----|---------------|---------------|--------|\n35\t| A1-LoRA (Pi0) | 800 | 0% | 91.5% | 0.4% (3/732) | 99.6% (729/732) | eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun |\n36\t| LoRA baseline (Pi0) | 200 | 0% | 82% | 0.5% (~1/164) | 99.4% (~163/164) | eval_lora_baseline_object_v11 |\n37\t| Full-FT baseline (Pi0) | 200 | 0.5% | 83% | 需补充 | 需补充 | eval_baseline_v11_object |\n38\t| Pi0.5 baseline (3-seed) | 600 | 74.7% | 26.8% | 0.5% (1/200 in s0) | 98.2% (s0) | eval_pi05_safelibero_object_v11 + s1 + s2 |\n39\t| **Pi0.5 + A1 (10K, s0, λ=0.005)** | — | 47% | 58% | ~100% (0% frozen) | ~0% | ROADMAP D016 |\n40\t| **Pi0.5 + A1 (10K, s0, λ=0.01)** | — | 49% | 56.5% | ~100% (0% frozen) | ~0% | ROADMAP D016 |\n41\t\n42\t**Fake Safe 判定标准：** safe episode 中 displacement < 0.1mm（即 arm 几乎完全静止）\n43\t\n44\t**A1-LoRA 详细位移分布（800 eps, 732 safe）：**\n45\t- < 1µm: 541 episodes (73.9%)\n46\t- 1µm – 0.1mm: 188 episodes (25.7%)\n47\t- 0.1mm – 1mm: 3 episodes (0.4%) ← real safe\n48\t- \\> 1mm: 0 episodes\n49\t\n50\t**关键结论：** Pi0 系方法 CAR 82-91.5% 看似优秀，但 99%+ 的 \"safe\" episodes 是因为机械臂完全停止运动（displacement < 0.1mm），而非学会了绕开障碍物。Pi0.5+A1 虽然 CAR 较低（56-58%），但 0% frozen 意味着所有安全行为都是真实的碰撞避免。\n51\t\n52\t---\n53\t\n54\t## Table 3 (Claim 3): Oracle Comparison — Runtime Refinement 无效\n55\t\n56\t**核心论点：** 即使使用 ground-truth SDF 做 runtime gradient refinement，也无法解决 fake safety 问题，证明 inference-time 优化路线不可行。\n57\t\n58\t| Method | TSR | CAR | Fake Safe Rate | Refine Count/ep | Source |\n59\t|--------|-----|-----|---------------|----------------|--------|\n60\t| Oracle-adaptive (GT SDF) | 0% | 75.0% | 98.3% (118/120) | 14.2 | oracle_true_gt_adaptive_alpha_v11 |\n61\t| Oracle-fixed α=0.005 (GT SDF) | 0% | 73.1% | 98.3% (115/117) | 14.8 | oracle_true_gt_fixed_alpha_v11 |\n62\t| Oracle-feature (GT SDF) | 0% | 76.9% | 96.7% (119/123) | 241.7 | oracle_true_gt_feature_v11 |\n63\t| A3 no-force (learned SDF) | 0% | 74.5% | — | 0 (never triggered) | eval_a3_v11_object |\n64\t| LoRA baseline (no refine) | 0% | 82% | 99.4% | N/A | eval_lora_baseline_object_v11 |\n65\t| Full-FT baseline (no refine) | 0.5% | 83% | 需补充 | N/A | eval_baseline_v11_object |\n66\t\n67\t**Oracle 实验参数：**\n68\t- n=160 episodes (4 tasks × 40 eps), seed 0\n69\t- GT SDF = 真实场景的 signed distance field\n70\t- Adaptive: 动态调整 refinement strength\n71\t- Fixed: α=0.005 固定步长\n72\t- Feature-space: 在 feature 层面做梯度修正（每步都 refine，avg 241.7/ep）\n73\t\n74\t**关键结论：**\n75\t1. Oracle refinement（GT SDF）vs 无 refine 的 LoRA baseline：CAR 反而**更低**（73-77% vs 82%），说明 refinement 在破坏策略\n76\t2. 所有 Oracle 方法 fake_safe_rate 仍高达 96-98%，GT SDF 都救不了\n77\t3. A3（learned SDF）的 refine 从未被触发（SDF 预测值未达阈值），实际退化为 baseline\n78\t4. Feature-space oracle 每步都 refine（241.7/ep vs action-space 14.2/ep），梯度幅度极小（0.004-0.006 vs action-space 0.18-0.49），但结果无显著差异\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## Table 4: TSR-CAR Scatter 数据点（Fig 3 素材）\n83\t\n84\t用于绘制 TSR vs CAR 散点图，展示各方法在 task success 和 collision avoidance 两个维度上的 trade-off。\n85\t\n86\t```\n87\tmethod_name, TSR, CAR, n_episodes, marker_style_suggestion\n88\t# --- Pi0.5 系列 (高 TSR, 低-中 CAR) ---\n89\tPi0.5 baseline s0 (seed 7), 0.73, 0.28, 200, blue_circle\n90\tPi0.5 baseline s1, 0.76, 0.25, 200, blue_circle\n91\tPi0.5 baseline s2, 0.75, 0.275, 200, blue_circle\n92\tPi0.5+A1 λ=0.005 (10K s0), 0.47, 0.58, -, red_star\n93\tPi0.5+A1 λ=0.01 (10K s0), 0.49, 0.565, -, red_star\n94\t# --- Pi0 系列 (低 TSR, 高 CAR — fake safety) ---\n95\tPi0 LoRA baseline, 0.0, 0.82, 200, gray_triangle\n96\tPi0 Full-FT baseline, 0.005, 0.83, 200, gray_triangle\n97\tA1-LoRA (Pi0), 0.0, 0.915, 800, orange_diamond\n98\t# --- Oracle 系列 (低 TSR, 中-高 CAR — GT SDF 也无效) ---\n99\tOracle adaptive (GT SDF), 0.0, 0.75, 160, green_square_hollow\n100\tOracle fixed α=0.005 (GT SDF), 0.0, 0.731, 160, green_square_hollow\n101\tOracle feature-space (GT SDF), 0.0, 0.769, 160, green_square_hollow\n102\t# --- A3 Gradient Refine ---\n103\tA3 no-force (learned SDF), 0.0, 0.745, 200, purple_pentagon\n104\tA3 M024fix, 0.0, 0.771, 200, purple_pentagon_hollow\n105\t# --- Spatial 系列 ---\n106\tPi0.5 spatial (seed 7), 0.575, 0.13, 200, blue_circle_hollow\n107\tA1-LoRA spatial, 0.001, 0.008, 200, orange_diamond_hollow\n108\tLoRA baseline spatial, 0.0, 0.0, 200, gray_triangle_hollow\n109\tFull-FT baseline spatial, 0.00375, 0.0, 800, gray_triangle_hollow\n110\t```\n111\t\n112\t**Fig 3 设计建议：**\n113\t- X 轴: TSR (Task Success Rate), Y 轴: CAR (Collision Avoidance Rate)\n114\t- 理想区域 = 右上角（高 TSR + 高 CAR）\n115\t- Pi0 系聚集在左上（高 CAR 但 0 TSR — 全是 fake safety）\n116\t- Pi0.5 baseline 在右下（高 TSR 但低 CAR）\n117\t- **Pi0.5+A1 是唯一向右上移动的方法**（中等 TSR + 中等 CAR，且 0% frozen）\n118\t- 可用虚线标注 \"Pareto front\"\n119\t- 用不同填充/颜色区分 fake safe (空心) vs real safe (实心) 方法\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## 补充数据：Per-task CAR 分解\n124\t\n125\t| Method | task0 (orange_juice) | task1 (choc_pudding) | task2 (milk) | task3 (bbq_sauce) |\n126\t|--------|---------------------|---------------------|-------------|-------------------|\n127\t| Full-FT baseline | 76% | 90% | 88% | 78% |\n128\t| LoRA baseline | 96% | 46% | 98% | 88% |\n129\t| A1-LoRA (800ep) | 96% | 82% | 97% | 91% |\n130\t| A3 no-force | 84% | 48% | 82% | 84% |\n131\t| Oracle adaptive | 82.5% | 55% | 77.5% | 85% |\n132\t| Oracle fixed | 85% | 50% | 77.5% | 80% |\n133\t| Oracle feature | 90% | 47.5% | 82.5% | 87.5% |\n134\t\n135\t**观察：** task1 (chocolate_pudding) 是所有方法的难点，CAR 普遍最低。可能该任务的碰撞场景更 challenging。\n136\t\n137\t---\n138\t\n139\t## 待补充项\n140\t\n141\t1. **seed 1/2 的 30K eval 结果** — 训练完成但 SSH failure 未跑 eval，需重连服务器执行\n142\t2. **Full-FT baseline 的 fake_safe_rate** — registry 中无该字段，需补跑位移分析\n143\t3. **Pi0.5+A1 10K eval 的详细位移分布** — 证实 0% frozen 的 displacement 分布\n144\t4. **Pi0.5 baseline s1/s2 的 fake_safe_rate** — 仅 s0 有数据 (98.2%)\n145\t5. **Pi0.5+A1 30K eval** — s0 已训练 30K，需对比 10K vs 30K 的 TSR/CAR 变化\n146\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ABmwNtxoSvH6DMETU8kjFH","session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"1002faac-1a54-43bb-9ea7-8bdd14b2bb18","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:36:34.726Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01C7MBSyVfLwqzR9K2kPLKBD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SzJgRpakVmGTQ26MbPjsQK","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work Review","prompt":"You are **Reviewer R2** for a robotics/ML conference (CoRL). Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Venue Standards (CoRL)\n- Rating scale: 1-10 (10=seminal, 8-9=strong accept, 7=accept, 6=marginal accept, 5=marginal reject, 4=reject, 3=clear reject, 1-2=strong reject)\n- Acceptance rate: ~40%\n- Evaluation dimensions: Originality, Quality (technical soundness), Clarity, Significance, Relevance to robot learning, Limitations\n- Papers must demonstrate relevance to robot learning through intent or outcome\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title:** \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: Decomposing Collision Avoidance into Implicit Demonstrations and Explicit Geometric Supervision\"\n\nThe paper studies collision avoidance in VLA models on SafeLIBERO benchmark. Three claims:\n\n1. **Fake Safety:** Pi0 with SDF loss achieves 91.5% CAR but TSR=0% — action collapse, not avoidance. Propose dfCAR metric that filters out frozen episodes. Robust across δ∈[2mm,100mm].\n\n2. **Decomposing Avoidance Sources:** LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demos = dominant avoidance signal (+29pp CAR). SDF auxiliary loss only adds at high λ=0.1 (+15.5pp, p<0.02), not at low λ.\n\n3. **Two-Phase Training:** SDF pre-training → task fine-tuning achieves CAR=66%, TSR=40% (2-seed mean).\n\n## Paper Structure (7 pages)\n- **Abstract:** Claims fake safety identification, decomposition framework, two-phase curriculum\n- **Section 1 (Intro):** Motivates the problem, presents 3 findings\n- **Section 2 (Related Work):** 4 short paragraphs covering VLA Safety Evaluation, SDFs in Robotics, Safety-Capability Tradeoffs, Curriculum/Multi-Phase Training. All citations are \"[?]\" placeholders.\n- **Section 3 (Method):** Problem setup, dfCAR definition (Eq. 1), SDF loss (Eq. 2), Two-phase protocol\n- **Section 4 (Experiments):** 8 subsections with 8 tables\n- **Section 5 (Discussion):** Decomposition vs Redundancy, High LoRA Variance, Two-Phase Promise, Scene-Dependent Effects, Limitations (5 items)\n- **Section 6 (Conclusion):** Summary of 3 findings + guidance\n\n## Detailed Content for Related Work Assessment\n\n**Section 2 full text:**\n- VLA Safety Evaluation: SafeLIBERO [?] introduced CAR. Paper claims to identify systematic contamination by action collapse and propose dfCAR.\n- SDFs in Robotics: SDFs in motion planning [??]. Vision-learned SDFs for avoidance [?]. Paper uses SDF as training-time signal, not runtime.\n- Safety-Capability Tradeoffs: Safe RL literature [?]. Paper's finding echoes conservatism-capability tradeoff but from different mechanism (demo learning vs explicit safety objective).\n- Curriculum/Multi-Phase Training: Progressive training [?]. Paper's two-phase = novel application of curriculum learning to VLA safety.\n\n**CRITICAL: ALL CITATIONS ARE PLACEHOLDERS \"[?]\"** — no actual references in the paper.\n\n## Key Experimental Numbers for Novelty Assessment\n- Fake safety: A1 CAR=91%, TSR=0%, EE disp=0.005mm in safe eps\n- dfCAR: threshold-robust across 3 orders of magnitude\n- LoRA implicit signal: +29pp CAR over baseline\n- SDF dose-response: flat at λ≤0.01, jumps +15.5pp at λ=0.1\n- Two-phase: CAR=66%, TSR=40% vs LoRA-only TSR=5%\n- Cross-scene inconsistency: SDF redundant in object_pudding, additive in spatial_bowl\n\n## Experiment Coverage Gaps (from review_context.yaml)\n- OpenVLA experiment BLOCKED → only 2 model families\n- Only 2 seeds for two-phase\n- spatial_bowl: 1 seed per condition\n- LoRA seed2 low CAR (44%) drives high variance (SD=6.5pp)\n- No exploration of different Phase 1 durations or λ values\n\n## YOUR TASK\n\nWrite a detailed review focusing on **Novelty and Related Work**. Evaluate:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment:**\n   - Is \"fake safety\" / action collapse genuinely novel? Action collapse is well-known in RL and robot learning.\n   - Is dfCAR a significant metric contribution? It's essentially filtering by displacement — how different from simply reporting TSR alongside CAR?\n   - Is the decomposition into implicit (demo) vs explicit (SDF) signals a novel insight? Or obvious in retrospect?\n   - Is the dose-response finding (threshold effect at λ=0.1) novel or expected?\n   - Is the two-phase curriculum genuinely novel for VLA safety?\n\n2. **Related Work Completeness:**\n   - ALL citations are \"[?]\" placeholders — this is a major formatting/completeness issue\n   - Missing related work areas:\n     * Safe reinforcement learning (constrained MDPs, Lagrangian methods, etc.)\n     * Other VLA safety benchmarks beyond SafeLIBERO\n     * Action collapse / mode collapse in generative models / VLAs\n     * Reward shaping / auxiliary losses in RL\n     * Other geometric representations for safety (not just SDF)\n     * Sim-to-real transfer for safety evaluation\n   - Is the positioning relative to safe RL adequate?\n   - Is the curriculum learning framing appropriately contextualized?\n\n3. **Contribution Significance:**\n   - For CoRL (~40% acceptance): is this sufficient contribution?\n   - Is the paper primarily empirical observation or methodological contribution?\n   - The main \"method\" contributions (dfCAR, SDF loss, two-phase) are relatively simple — is the insight enough?\n   - Is the scope (single benchmark, 2 model families, 1 main scene) sufficient for the claims?\n\n4. **Framing and Positioning:**\n   - The title claims \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation\" — does the paper deliver?\n   - Is the \"decomposition framework\" really a framework or just an empirical observation?\n   - The paper acknowledges many limitations honestly — does this help or hurt?\n\n5. **Writing Quality:**\n   - Is the paper well-organized?\n   - Are the claims appropriately hedged?\n   - Is the discussion balanced?\n\nOutput your review in this format:\n\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Strengths\n[Bulleted list, 4-6 items]\n\n### Weaknesses\n[Bulleted list, 4-8 items, each with specific evidence]\n\n### Questions for Authors\n[3-5 specific questions]\n\n### Missing Related Work\n[Specific papers/areas that should be cited]\n\n### Minor Issues\n[Formatting, writing, etc.]\n\n### Scores\n- Originality: [1-4] (1=poor, 2=fair, 3=good, 4=excellent)\n- Significance: [1-4]\n- Clarity: [1-4]\n- Overall: [1-10] with justification\n- Confidence: [1-5] (1=low, 5=expert)\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":608,"cache_read_input_tokens":63471,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":608},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"300af2a7-bc34-45bd-9683-8d068f2efde2"}
