{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016KajGJjyVdxa4vTKK4j5dE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\begin{abstract}\n2\tVision-Language-Action (VLA) models generate manipulation trajectories from visual observations and language instructions, but frequently collide with non-target objects in cluttered workspaces. Existing collision-safe approaches either apply post-hoc corrections to already-generated trajectories or rely on reinforcement learning without geometric reasoning, leaving the VLA's internal representations collision-ignorant. We propose ColliForce-VLA, which integrates a differentiable workspace Signed Distance Field (SDF) into the VLA forward pass for collision-aware action generation. Two lightweight modules, an SDF Decoder (${\\sim}$395K parameters) and an End-Effector Extractor (${\\sim}$263K parameters), are attached to the action expert of $\\pi_0$, a 3.5B-parameter flow-matching VLA. During training, for near-collision samples, we compute the SDF gradient in feature space and perform gradient ascent to produce collision-corrected action targets; a refinement loss trains the LoRA parameters (${\\sim}$33.5M) to reproduce these targets directly. At inference, the default path requires only the base model with trained LoRA adapters, adding no extra modules or computation. On the SafeLIBERO benchmark, ColliForce-VLA achieves a Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR) of \\textbf{[TODO]}\\% on \\textit{spatial\\_bowl} and \\textbf{[TODO]}\\% on \\textit{object\\_pudding}, improving over the LoRA baseline by \\textbf{[TODO]} and \\textbf{[TODO]} percentage points respectively, while maintaining Task Success Rates (TSR) of \\textbf{[TODO]}\\% and \\textbf{[TODO]}\\%. Ablation studies confirm that the gradient-guided refinement provides \\textbf{[TODO]} percentage points additional CAR gain beyond auxiliary SDF supervision alone.\n3\t\\end{abstract}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ABmwNtxoSvH6DMETU8kjFH","session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"0aeec1c7-8cce-4702-b12f-e83db19f006c","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:36:40.880Z"}
