{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JAy1sbVVWmaqY7mEGa7dMg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tdream_id: dream_20260526T023936\n3\ttier: best\n4\toverall_score: weak reject\n5\ttimestamp: 2026-05-26T03:25:06.145215+00:00\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Dream Review Report — \"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation: When 98% of Collision Avoidance is an Illusion\"\n9\t\n10\t**Target venue**: CoRL 2026 (rating scale 1–10; acceptance rate ~28–33%)\n11\t**Review mode**: full (2 Reviewers → 4-step roundtable)\n12\t**dream_id**: 20260526T023936\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## 1  Roundtable Process Summary\n17\t\n18\t| Step | Description |\n19\t|------|-------------|\n20\t| Step 1 | Independent reviews: R1 (methods + experiments) and R2 (novelty + related work) |\n21\t| Step 2 | Cross-sharing: each reviewer read the other's review |\n22\t| Step 3 | Convergence discussion: areas of agreement/disagreement identified |\n23\t| Step 4 | This consolidated report |\n24\t\n25\t**Final scores**: R1 = 4/10, R2 = 4/10. Both maintained ratings after cross-reading.\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## 2  Paper Summary\n30\t\n31\tThe paper makes four claims:\n32\t\n33\t1. **Fake safety**: Standard CAR is contaminated by action collapse. A Pi0+SDF model (A1) reports 91.5% CAR, but 99.6% of \"safe\" episodes have obstacle displacement < 0.1 mm and TSR = 0%.\n34\t2. **dfCAR metric**: A displacement-filtered CAR that excludes frozen episodes (EE displacement < δ). Threshold-robust due to bimodal gap > 200 mm.\n35\t3. **SDF redundancy**: LoRA fine-tuning on collision-free demonstrations alone produces +29 pp genuine CAR. Adding SDF auxiliary loss contributes 0 additional pp across a 4-point λ curve (0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1). Confirmed across 2 scenes.\n36\t4. **Phase 2 persistence**: SDF training (10K steps) followed by 20K steps without SDF → model reverts to LoRA-only baseline. Zero persistent effect.\n37\t\n38\t---\n39\t\n40\t## 3  Consolidated Strengths (agreed by both reviewers)\n41\t\n42\t- **Quantitative rigor on the diagnostic claim (Claim 1)**: 800 episodes for A1, per-episode obstacle displacement analysis, dual evidence chain (obstacle displacement + TSR = 0%). The 99.6% fake safety rate is striking and communicates severity effectively.\n43\t- **dfCAR threshold robustness**: The bimodal gap (> 200 mm between frozen and active modes) makes dfCAR genuinely threshold-insensitive across δ ∈ [2, 200] mm. This is a clean property.\n44\t- **4-point λ dose-response curve**: Correct experimental design for testing dose-independence. Flat curve (slope = −0.3, R² = 0.12) across a 20× range is convincing within its scope.\n45\t- **Honest negative result reporting**: The paper does not hide the SDF redundancy finding or the catastrophic TSR collapse.\n46\t- **Clear writing and logical narrative arc**: The flow from fake safety → dfCAR → attribution → SDF redundancy is well-structured.\n47\t\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t## 4  Consolidated Weaknesses\n51\t\n52\t### 4.1  Statistical Power (R1 primary, R2 concurs)\n53\t\n54\tThe SDF redundancy claim (Claim 3) is the paper's headline finding but is critically underpowered:\n55\t\n56\t- **n = 3 seeds per condition**: The Welch t-test (Δ = −2.4 pp, p = 0.35) has very low power. The 95% CI on the LoRA-vs-SDF difference likely spans ~[−7, +2] pp, so the data cannot distinguish \"0 pp effect\" from \"5 pp effect.\"\n57\t- **No equivalence testing**: The paper claims \"SDF contributes 0 pp\" but uses absence-of-significance as evidence-of-absence. A formal TOST equivalence test with a pre-registered margin is needed; current n almost certainly lacks power to pass one.\n58\t- **Phase 2 uses only 2 seeds**: Claiming \"zero persistent effect\" from n = 2 is statistically irresponsible.\n59\t- **spatial_bowl is single-seed per condition**: The cross-scene \"replication\" (Δ = +2 pp, n.s.) is effectively anecdotal.\n60\t\n61\t### 4.2  Circular SDF Redundancy Design (R2 primary, R1 concurs after cross-reading)\n62\t\n63\tThe paper establishes that EE-only SDF has fundamental structural defects (Section 4.7: misses arm-body collisions, gradient direction misaligned with action space). It then tests SDF redundancy using *only* EE-only SDF. This is circular: showing that a known-deficient method adds nothing is uninformative about whether geometric supervision in general is redundant. The paper cannot distinguish between:\n64\t\n65\t- \"Geometric supervision is fundamentally redundant for VLA collision avoidance\" (strong, novel)\n66\t- \"This particular EE-only SDF formulation is too limited to help\" (weak, expected)\n67\t\n68\tThe title and framing imply the strong claim; the evidence supports only the weak one.\n69\t\n70\t### 4.3  Narrow Experimental Scope vs. Broad Claims (both reviewers)\n71\t\n72\t- **2 model families** (Pi0, Pi0.5 — architecturally related, same family)\n73\t- **1 benchmark** (SafeLIBERO)\n74\t- **2 scenes** (object_pudding primarily; spatial_bowl single-seed)\n75\t- **Simulation only** (no real-robot validation)\n76\t- **OpenVLA blocked** (model download failures, acknowledged as limitation)\n77\t\n78\tThe title (\"Rethinking VLA Safety Evaluation\") and claims (\"SDF geometric supervision is redundant\") are stated at a generality the evidence cannot support. The mechanistic argument for Claim 1 (any frozen model gets high CAR) is general, but Claims 3–4 are specific to EE-only SDF on SafeLIBERO with Pi0-family models.\n79\t\n80\t### 4.4  Conceptual Novelty (R2 primary)\n81\t\n82\t- **\"Frozen robot = high safety score\"** is a specific instance of Goodhart's Law / specification gaming / reward hacking by inaction, extensively documented in safe RL literature (Amodei et al. 2016; Krakovna et al. 2020; Skalse et al. 2022). The observation is real but not conceptually new.\n83\t- **dfCAR** is the most straightforward possible fix: \"check if the robot moved before crediting it with safety.\" No alternative metrics explored, no connection to measurement theory or construct validity, no formal analysis of failure modes.\n84\t- **\"Demonstrations encode avoidance\"** is expected from imitation learning theory — if collision-free demonstrations are the training data, behavioral cloning learns collision-free behavior. The paper does not engage with IL literature (DAgger, MaxEntIRL, causal confusion).\n85\t\n86\t### 4.5  Missing Application to Published Methods (both reviewers)\n87\t\n88\tThe paper proposes dfCAR as a community metric but never applies it to any prior method (AEGIS, SafeVLA, CAPE, etc.). Demonstrating that dfCAR changes the relative ranking or conclusions about existing published safety methods would dramatically strengthen the practical impact. Without this, the metric's value is speculative.\n89\t\n90\t### 4.6  Reproducibility and Internal Consistency (R1 primary, R2 concurs)\n91\t\n92\t- **A1 checkpoint deleted**: The primary Claim 1 evidence (800 episodes) cannot be reproduced.\n93\t- **Internal metric inconsistency**: dfCAR is defined using EE displacement, but the A1 analysis uses obstacle displacement. Two different filtering paradigms are used without reconciliation.\n94\t\n95\t### 4.7  TSR Collapse Underanalyzed (both reviewers)\n96\t\n97\tFine-tuning produces +29 pp CAR but −68 pp TSR (73% → 6%). This catastrophic task performance collapse may be the most practically important finding — any method that destroys task success is unusable in deployment. Yet it receives minimal mechanistic analysis. Is this catastrophic forgetting? LoRA rank insufficiency? Distribution shift? The paper treats it as a footnote when it should be a central discussion point.\n98\t\n99\t---\n100\t\n101\t## 5  Related Work Gaps (R2)\n102\t\n103\tThe paper's related work section is thin relative to the breadth of its claims. Key missing areas:\n104\t\n105\t| Area | Missing References/Topics |\n106\t|------|--------------------------|\n107\t| Metric validity / Goodhart's Law | Specification gaming (Krakovna et al. 2020), reward hacking (Skalse et al. 2022) |\n108\t| Conservative/frozen policy failure | Offline RL conservatism (CQL, BCQ), risk-averse policy collapse |\n109\t| Safe RL | CPO (Achiam et al. 2017), Lagrangian CMDP methods |\n110\t| Full-body collision | Configuration-space distance fields, whole-body planning (MoveIt, TrajOpt) |\n111\t| IL theory on demonstration content | DAgger (Ross et al. 2011), MaxEntIRL (Ziebart et al. 2008), causal confusion (de Haan et al. 2019) |\n112\t| Phase 2 / curriculum learning | Scheduled auxiliary losses, progressive training (Bengio et al. 2009) |\n113\t| Other VLA safety benchmarks | RoboCasa, BEHAVIOR, or other safety-adjacent evaluations |\n114\t\n115\t---\n116\t\n117\t## 6  Experiment Coverage vs. Plan\n118\t\n119\t| Planned Experiment | Paper Status | Assessment |\n120\t|---|---|---|\n121\t| LoRA baseline 3-seed | 3 seeds reported (Table 1) | ✅ Complete |\n122\t| 3v3 LoRA vs SDF comparison | 3 seeds each reported (Table 2) | ✅ Complete (but underpowered) |\n123\t| 4-point λ dose curve | All 4 points reported (Table 3) | ✅ Complete (λ=0.1 has only 2 seeds) |\n124\t| Phase 2 ablation multi-seed | 2 seeds reported (Tables 6–7) | ⚠️ Marginal (n=2 for null claim) |\n125\t| spatial_bowl cross-scene SDF | Single-seed per condition (Table 5) | ⚠️ Underpowered (n=1) |\n126\t| spatial_bowl LoRA-only control | Reported (Table 5) | ⚠️ Single seed |\n127\t| dfCAR threshold sensitivity | 7 thresholds reported (Table 8) | ✅ Complete |\n128\t| A1 re-eval with EE displacement | Cancelled (checkpoint deleted) | ❌ Missing |\n129\t| OpenVLA eval | Blocked (download failures) | ❌ Missing |\n130\t| dfCAR on published methods | Not attempted | ❌ Missing |\n131\t\n132\t---\n133\t\n134\t## 7  Questions for Authors (consolidated, prioritized)\n135\t\n136\t1. **Equivalence testing**: Have you considered TOST to formally test SDF redundancy? What equivalence margin would you pre-register, and does n=3 provide adequate power?\n137\t2. **SDF circularity**: Your oracle experiments show EE-only SDF fails structurally. You then test SDF redundancy using only EE-only SDF. How do you distinguish \"geometric supervision is redundant\" from \"this EE-only formulation is too broken to help\"?\n138\t3. **dfCAR on published methods**: Can you apply dfCAR to AEGIS or any published safety method's per-episode data? Even one such demonstration would substantially strengthen the metric contribution.\n139\t4. **TSR collapse mechanism**: Is the 73% → 6% TSR collapse catastrophic forgetting, LoRA rank limitation, or inherent safety-task tradeoff? Have you tried standard mitigations (EWC, replay, lower LR)?\n140\t5. **Bimodal gap universality**: Is the > 200 mm gap a property of SafeLIBERO workspace dimensions? Would it hold on benchmarks with smaller workspaces?\n141\t6. **A1 reproducibility**: Can EE displacement be extracted from existing 800-episode logs (if joint positions were recorded)?\n142\t\n143\t---\n144\t\n145\t## 8  Scores\n146\t\n147\t### R1 (Methods + Experiments)\n148\t| Dimension | Score |\n149\t|-----------|-------|\n150\t| Soundness | 2/4 |\n151\t| Presentation | 3/4 |\n152\t| Contribution | 2/4 |\n153\t| Overall | **4/10** |\n154\t| Confidence | 4/5 |\n155\t\n156\t### R2 (Novelty + Related Work)\n157\t| Dimension | Score |\n158\t|-----------|-------|\n159\t| Novelty & Significance | 2/4 |\n160\t| Presentation | 3/4 |\n161\t| Overall | **4/10** |\n162\t| Confidence | 4/5 |\n163\t\n164\t### Consolidated\n165\t| Dimension | Score |\n166\t|-----------|-------|\n167\t| **Overall Rating** | **4/10 (Weak Reject)** |\n168\t| Confidence | 4/5 |\n169\t\n170\t---\n171\t\n172\t## 9  Meta-Review / AC Summary\n173\t\n174\tThis paper identifies a real and practically relevant problem: standard CAR is contaminated by action collapse in VLA models, and the proposed dfCAR metric is a clean, threshold-robust correction. The 99.6% fake safety rate on Pi0+SDF (A1) is a striking empirical finding.\n175\t\n176\tHowever, the paper falls short of the CoRL acceptance bar for three interconnected reasons:\n177\t\n178\t1. **The headline negative finding (SDF redundancy) is both underpowered and confounded.** With n=3 seeds and no equivalence testing, the data cannot formally support \"zero effect.\" Worse, the SDF variant tested (EE-only) is already shown to be structurally deficient within the same paper, creating a circular argument.\n179\t\n180\t2. **The experimental scope is narrow relative to the generality of claims.** Two architecturally related models, one benchmark, two scenes (one single-seed), simulation only, and two blocked/cancelled experiments (OpenVLA, A1 re-eval) do not support claims about \"VLA Safety Evaluation\" in general.\n181\t\n182\t3. **The conceptual novelty is limited.** The core observation (\"inaction inflates non-event metrics\") is a well-known pattern in evaluation methodology. dfCAR is the most straightforward fix. The paper does not engage with extensive related literatures on specification gaming, imitation learning theory, or metric validity.\n183\t\n184\t**Path to acceptance**: (a) Apply dfCAR to published methods to demonstrate field-wide impact. (b) Test a non-deficient SDF variant (full-body or multi-link) to disambiguate the redundancy claim. (c) Use equivalence testing with adequate sample size. (d) Expand to at least one additional VLA architecture. (e) Analyze the TSR collapse mechanism. (f) Engage with specification gaming, IL theory, and safe RL literatures.\n185\t\n186\t**Estimated acceptance probability at CoRL 2026 in current form: 10–15%.**\n187\t\n188\t---\n189\t\n190\t*Review conducted 2026-05-26. Two independent reviewers (R1: methods/experiments, R2: novelty/related work) with full 4-step roundtable protocol.*\n191\t\n192\t---\n193\t\n194\t## 引用验证结果\n195\t\n196\t**统计**: 40 篇文献 / 29 处引用 / 在线验证 40/40 篇\n197\t\n198\t### 问题 (24)\n199\t\n200\t- ⚠️ `liu2023libero` — 元数据不匹配: first_author: bib=liu vs api=feng\n201\t- ❌ `karwowski2024goodhart` — 在线验证未找到匹配（疑似虚假引用）: best match similarity 0.29 below threshold 0.82\n202\t- ⚠️ `geoaware2025` — 元数据不匹配: first_author: bib=abouzeid vs api=ali\n203\t- ❌ `stemvla2026` — 在线验证未找到匹配（疑似虚假引用）: no results from any source\n204\t- ❌ `evo02025` — 在线验证未找到匹配（疑似虚假引用）: best match similarity 0.31 below threshold 0.82\n205\t- ⚠️ `vasilopoulos2023ramp` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n206\t- ⚠️ `chen2026cssdfnet` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n207\t- ⚠️ `jacquet2025neuralnmpc` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n208\t- ⚠️ `chen2025samp` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n209\t- ⚠️ `ruan2025profrobot` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n210\t- ⚠️ `depthvla2025` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n211\t- ⚠️ `li2025qdepth` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n212\t- ⚠️ `li2025spatialforcing` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n213\t- ⚠️ `3dcavla2025` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n214\t- ⚠️ `geoaware2025` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n215\t- ⚠️ `spatialvla2025` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n216\t- ⚠️ `gstvla2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n217\t- ⚠️ `stemvla2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n218\t- ⚠️ `stvla2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n219\t- ⚠️ `evo02025` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n220\t- ⚠️ `savla2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n221\t- ⚠️ `augvla3d2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n222\t- ⚠️ `evodepth2026` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n223\t- ⚠️ `chen2026dfmvla` — 在 .bib 中但正文未引用\n224\t\n225\t### ✅ 通过 (35)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01ABmwNtxoSvH6DMETU8kjFH","session_id":"9c2499d0-d3bb-4c09-8644-35391fa8435e","uuid":"b17a0fbf-e3f3-41df-bcd5-ec50eb7c63f6","timestamp":"2026-05-26T03:36:51.903Z"}
